://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17832206?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/diomonogatari","html_url":"https://github.com/diomonogatari","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diomonogatari/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diomonogatari/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diomonogatari/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diomonogatari/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diomonogatari/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diomonogatari/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diomonogatari/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diomonogatari/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diomonogatari/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-10T17:44:26Z","updated_at":"2026-08-10T17:44:26Z","body":"I was following the breadcrumbs on this one and decided to leave this one here as it is the original issue that caused the change on the VMA flag https://github.com/GPUOpen-LibrariesAndSDKs/VulkanMemoryAllocator/issues/338\r\n\r\nI have no idea if this will be a problem for Godot after reverting the flag to `0` and if it is I also have no idea how big the subset of affected people will be.\r\n\r\nSo the main question that I'm wondering as someone that has 0 knowledge of graphics programming at hardware level is, would reverting the default back to `0` create a ticking time-bomb?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5243837345/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6048424681","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120603#issuecomment-6048424681","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120603","id":6048424681,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABaIOi6Q","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-07T22:47:54Z","updated_at":"2026-10-07T22:47:54Z","body":"This might be acceptable as a temporary workaround. But ultimately, we need to understand what is causing VMA to exceed the allocation limit. VMA should only be making a few allocations and then suballocating from them as needed. Therefore, it seems like We are doing something that is causing VMA to make more allocations than it should. \r\n\r\nWe need to figure out what that is and fix it. This change just masks the problem. But it leads to undefined behaviour.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6048424681/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6107182